1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,421
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,888
[Arthur] <i>There's no place</i>
<i>for justice in Ardiente!</i>

3
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>What do we have?</i>
<i>Violence, bloodshed, and wealth!</i>

4
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:20,478
<i>And that's what I'm going</i>
<i>to take from you!</i>

5
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:23,356
<i>Ivy isn't here! She's not here!</i>

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:27,736
<i>Put Ivy Aguas on the phone.</i>

7
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:30,739
[muffled] <i>Hon! Hon!</i>

8
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:33,825
[Arthur] <i>Think twice about</i>
<i>everything you're going to do.</i>

9
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:37,996
<i>You don't want to marry</i>
<i>a corpse, now do you?</i>

10
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,082
[Jepoy] <i>I know you met</i>
<i>with Julio Ardiente.</i>

11
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,209
<i>What did you two talk about?</i>
<i>Will you sell Jaguar out?</i>

12
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,003
-[Rufo] <i>Will you rat me out?</i>
-[Jepoy] <i>Why not?</i>

13
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,546
[Rufo] <i>Well, I guess I have no choice.</i>

14
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:47,464
<i>Help!</i>

15
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:50,133
<i>Jaguar! I saw him talking</i>
<i>to Julio Ardiente.</i>

16
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,594
[man] <i>The boss is asking</i>
<i>what reward you want.</i>

17
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:53,470
<i>Money or weapons?</i>

18
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,221
<i>I want to be part of your group.</i>

19
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,973
[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy? Ivy.</i>

20
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,350
-[muffled screaming]
-<i>Ivy?</i>

21
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,187
[Ivy crying] <i>Why did he kidnap me?</i>

22
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,564
[Arnaldo] <i>Forgive me.</i>
<i>This is all my fault.</i>

23
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:05,774
[grunts]

24
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:08,568
<i>So, your informant's not responding, huh?</i>

25
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:11,696
<i>Maybe Jaguar has already intercepted him.</i>

26
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:16,868
<i>I want you to mount a manhunt</i>
<i>against this hoodlum Jaguar.</i>

27
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:20,121
<i>I want you to find him,</i>
<i>catch him, and kill him.</i>

28
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:21,456
[Raul] <i>Welcome to my group.</i>

29
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:23,208
<i>From now on, that will be your uniform.</i>

30
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>There's one thing I ask of you.</i>

31
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,419
<i>I just want you to be loyal to me.</i>

32
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:29,047
<i>Then you'll get everything you want.</i>

33
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,173
[Jepoy] <i>Loud and clear, boss.</i>

34
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,883
[Arnaldo] <i>We want our wedding</i>
<i>to happen soon.</i>

35
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:33,718
<i>-How soon?</i>
<i>-Next week.</i>

36
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,762
<i>We can make that happen. And don't worry.</i>

37
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:39,641
<i>I will make sure nothing will</i>
<i>get in the way of your wedding.</i>

38
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,694
Diego, I'll leave it up to you
to explain to Mom.

39
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:52,904
[tense music playing]

40
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:56,491
[Ivy] Don't let anyone find out
about what happened to me.

41
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:58,493
Okay, Ivy.

42
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:02,622
Thank you for understanding, Diego.

43
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:05,458
I'll call you again later.

44
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:09,337
Ivy, please take care.

45
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:17,428
Diego?

46
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:19,973
Was that Lily?

47
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,100
Uh… Yes, Auntie.

48
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,395
She says not to worry. She's doing okay.

49
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:27,939
That's great news.

50
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:33,528
All right, we'll be off, okay?

51
00:02:33,611 --> 00:02:35,780
Okay. Take care.

52
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:37,699
Let's go.

53
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:38,783
Anna.

54
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:42,495
Jepoy.

55
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:54,048
Don't bother coming back
until you have Arthur's body.

56
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,050
I'll pay you whatever you want

57
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:58,177
as long as you kill that bastard.

58
00:02:58,261 --> 00:02:59,554
Understood, Mayor.

59
00:03:01,472 --> 00:03:03,766
[sinister music playing]

60
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:07,812
Grandpa.

61
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,647
How long have you been there?

62
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:13,443
-Uh… I was talking--
-Arnaldo…

63
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:19,032
There's no need for you
to stutter or cover this up.

64
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:20,116
[scoffs]

65
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:23,161
Because I already know
what happened to Miss Aguas.

66
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:25,747
Now,

67
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:30,919
what I want to know
is who was behind this.

68
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:33,755
Do you think…

69
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:35,965
it's Diego?

70
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:40,470
[tense music playing]

71
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:43,806
That bastard.

72
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,642
[Arnaldo breathing sharply]

73
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,269
Follow him.

74
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,443
[Fernan] That was delicious, Loring.

75
00:03:55,526 --> 00:03:56,611
-Thank you so much.
-[Pandoy chuckles]

76
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,613
-[Loring] No problem.
-[Pandoy] You know you're always

77
00:03:58,696 --> 00:03:59,864
-welcome here.
-[Loring] That's right.

78
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,991
Hey, go straight home, okay?

79
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,952
-Don't go wandering off, okay?
-They're…

80
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:04,827
-What?
-They're asking us…

81
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:05,662
-[Arnaldo] Diego!
-[Loring] Oh!

82
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,580
-…to come drink with them.
-[Loring] Hold on.

83
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:08,539
-It's the mayor.
-[Arnaldo] Diego!

84
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:09,874
[ominous music playing]

85
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:10,959
[Loring] Oh.

86
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:12,669
-Where's Diego?
-[Loring] Um…

87
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:14,796
-What brings you here, Mayor?
-[Arnaldo] Where's Diego?!

88
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:15,713
Diego!

89
00:04:15,797 --> 00:04:16,881
-[Loring] Uh…
-Get out of there!

90
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:18,383
-Mayor. Mayor.
-Looks like…

91
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,551
You had too much to drink, Mayor.

92
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:23,304
-Diego!
-[Fernan] Calm down, Mayor.

93
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,847
[Pandoy] Good evening, Mayor.

94
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,183
-Mayor…
-[Arnaldo] Bring me Diego.

95
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,393
-[Pandoy] Mayor…
-Arnaldo!

96
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,689
You think I don't know what you did?

97
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:34,440
What are you doing here?

98
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:36,276
You had Arthur kidnap Ivy.

99
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,904
-What are you talking about?
-I know all your plans.

100
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:42,824
You did that so I'd lose
my focus on the campaign.

101
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:44,575
[scoffs]

102
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,704
All this time! How could I be so stupid?!

103
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:49,747
During the debate… In the restaurant…

104
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:51,332
You were behind everything.

105
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:53,209
-Well, now, I'm here.
-[Marlon] Mayor.

106
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,585
-Why?! What?!
-[Diego] Batch! Batch! Batch!

107
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:57,547
All of you! You're all to blame!

108
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:01,301
All of you. Everything that's happening…

109
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,470
Why didn't I think of this before?!

110
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:06,222
It's you!

111
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,099
You did all that!

112
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,852
-Go home.
-[Arnaldo laughs in disbelief]

113
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,313
-Just go home.
-Yes, I will go home

114
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:14,981
because I have a life to destroy.

115
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,065
But before that,

116
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:19,193
I want everyone to know that
I'm aware of what you're doing.

117
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,154
Especially you.

118
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,282
You can't stop our wedding.

119
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:28,786
Don't forget that. And not you!
Not you! Not you!

120
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:32,040
Not you can stop me from being
the governor of this town.

121
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,334
Not you.

122
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:38,755
It's me.

123
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,802
I'll put a stop to all your plans.

124
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:49,891
Bullshit!

125
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,934
[Arnaldo chuckles]

126
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:55,772
[tense music playing]

127
00:05:58,858 --> 00:05:59,859
[car engine starts]

128
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:11,829
[music stops]

129
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,124
[tense music playing]

130
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,292
Jaguar.

131
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,960
[Emilia sighs]

132
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:20,880
I just don't want Papa, Arnaldo,

133
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:23,007
and Ivy Aguas keeping secrets from me.

134
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:26,552
I've been telling you.
You should choose me.

135
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,554
I won't keep secrets from you.

136
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:32,809
For whatever it's worth,
thank you so much for listening.

137
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:35,561
You have my undivided attention, Emilia.

138
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,480
I'm not like your husband.

139
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:40,316
<i>He's not there when you need him most.</i>

140
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:42,360
He won't listen to me anyway.

141
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,112
<i>He'll just laugh at me.</i>

142
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,613
<i>That's how people are</i>

143
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:48,116
when they aren't interested to listen.

144
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:49,617
They won't pay attention to you.

145
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:50,952
[Raul] <i>Go ahead.</i>

146
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:52,787
Tell me everything you want to say.

147
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,248
I'm here to listen.

148
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:56,791
[chuckles]

149
00:06:57,458 --> 00:06:58,918
Thank you, Jaguar.

150
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:02,088
[sinister music playing]

151
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:09,554
[ominous music playing]

152
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:10,638
[pulls handbrake]

153
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:22,692
<i>Who do you think is capable</i>
<i>of leading this town?</i>

154
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:26,779
<i>Aside from us, the Ardientes?</i>
<i>Who else? Tell us! Who?!</i>

155
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,449
<i>Me.</i>

156
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:33,244
<i>I will run for governor</i>
<i>against you, Arnaldo.</i>

157
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,495
<i>Ivy, be careful.</i>

158
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,582
[sinister music playing]

159
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,502
[Arnaldo] <i>You can't help</i>
<i>but be jealous of me, can you?</i>

160
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,255
<i>Ever since we were kids,</i>
<i>you've always wanted what I had.</i>

161
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:47,717
<i>Mom's love, Grandpa's love,</i>

162
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:49,719
<i>and Ivy.</i>

163
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:52,805
<i>Hon?</i>

164
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,058
<i>Arnaldo.</i>

165
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,727
-[grunts]
-[Ivy] <i>Arnaldo!</i>

166
00:07:58,478 --> 00:07:59,645
<i>Arnaldo, enough!</i>

167
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,772
<i>If you don't believe me,</i>

168
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,941
<i>if you think I'm betraying you…</i>

169
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:05,610
<i>I guess, Arnaldo,</i>

170
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:07,820
<i>let's just stop this.</i>

171
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:10,990
<i>We should call off our wedding.</i>

172
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:12,575
[tense music playing]

173
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,243
[sobs]

174
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:16,329
No!

175
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:19,248
No! Ivy's mine!

176
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,209
She's all mine!

177
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:22,668
She's all mine!

178
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:24,378
She's mine!

179
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:26,005
She's mine, and she's mine alone.

180
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:28,174
No. No!

181
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,676
She's all mine.

182
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,261
She's mine alone.

183
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:36,974
Ivy's mine. Ivy's mine alone. Ivy's mine.

184
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:38,643
[exhales]

185
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:41,771
[sinister music playing]

186
00:08:45,483 --> 00:08:46,567
But…

187
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:48,903
But who… [mumbling]

188
00:08:48,986 --> 00:08:50,696
But who needs Ardiente?

189
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:54,158
Who needs Ardiente? Who needs power?

190
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:56,410
[exhales]

191
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:59,247
No. I don't need everything.

192
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,165
Ivy's all I need.

193
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,418
Ivy's all I need.

194
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:07,296
Ivy's all I need.

195
00:09:08,005 --> 00:09:09,423
Ivy's all I need.

196
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:11,801
Just Ivy.

197
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,886
Just Ivy.

198
00:09:15,137 --> 00:09:16,180
Just Ivy.

199
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:22,103
-[tense music playing]
-[whispering inaudibly]

200
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,274
Boss Jaguar says…

201
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,068
the Ardientes are hot on our trail.

202
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,987
He also heard that…

203
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,822
Julio Ardiente asked his friend
who has a private army

204
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:33,906
to hunt us down.

205
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:37,577
But we won't let them intimidate us.

206
00:09:38,035 --> 00:09:40,037
We'll continue with our casino operations.

207
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,249
Then, you'll need me in those operations.

208
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:48,462
-[tense music playing]
-[whispering inaudibly]

209
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:52,592
Madrigal…

210
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,636
The boss says you'll be guarding
the house for now.

211
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:59,890
And if you'll defy his orders,
then you'll be sorry.

212
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:05,980
[whispering inaudibly]

213
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,025
One more thing, Madrigal.

214
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:11,861
The boss' only wish…

215
00:10:12,486 --> 00:10:14,864
is for you to wear
the uniform he gave you.

216
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:17,491
[tense music playing]

217
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:29,587
Hon? Hon? Hon, hon, hon.

218
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,380
Get up. Get up. Get up.

219
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:33,090
-Wake up. Wake up. Get up.
-Hon?

220
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:34,550
-Let's go. Let's get out of here.
-Hon?

221
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,801
-Let's go. Let's go.
-Wait. Ouch! Ouch!

222
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,261
-Arnaldo!
-I'm… I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

223
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:38,095
-I'm sorry!
-What's going on?

224
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,722
No, no, no, no, no. This is--

225
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,682
No, no, no, no. We have to do this.

226
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:42,850
-What, hon?
-I have to do this.

227
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,644
I have to do this. We have to do this.

228
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,728
-Hon! What's happening?
-No, no, no.

229
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:46,896
-Hold on!
-Let's go. Let's go.

230
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,607
"Let's go" where? Where are we going? Why?

231
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:51,692
Let's leave Poblacion Ardiente.

232
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,319
-Huh?
-I'm begging you.

233
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:55,946
Let's leave everything behind.
Let's get away from my family.

234
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,698
Away from my family. Away from everyone

235
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,659
-who's trying to ruin us.
-Is my kidnapper here, hon?

236
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:01,160
-No, no, no, no, no!
-Is Arthur there?

237
00:11:01,243 --> 00:11:02,495
-I won't let anything
-Hon, is he back?

238
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:03,454
-happen to you.
-What's happening?!

239
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,580
No, no, no, no, no!

240
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:05,414
-Is he there?!
-I won't…

241
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:06,666
I won't let anything happen to you.

242
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:07,958
-Is my kidnapper there?
-It's just that I…

243
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:09,960
No, no, no, no! I thought… I thought…

244
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:11,045
I thought of something.

245
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,171
-What?
-Let's get away from here.

246
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:13,422
-What's happening?
-Let's start a new life

247
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:15,216
somewhere else, okay?

248
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:16,467
Let's start a new life somewhere else.

249
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:19,387
Away from my family.
Away from Poblacion Ardiente.

250
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:20,554
Away from everyone who's trying to ruin--

251
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:22,098
Away from this mess!

252
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:23,432
Let's go to Hong Kong.

253
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:26,727
Let's go to Hong Kong.
We will get married there.

254
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:27,978
Okay? I will marry you.

255
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,271
-[suspenseful music playing]
-I will…

256
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,400
I will marry you there, okay?

257
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:35,403
[stutters] Let's start
a new life somewhere.

258
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,946
Away. Away from this.

259
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:37,988
-Away from all of it.
-Hon.

260
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,156
Away from everything.

261
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,366
Away from everything.

262
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,660
Away from everything. Please?

263
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:43,744
-Hon.
-Please?

264
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:46,622
-Please? Let's go.
-Hon, hold on.

265
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:48,499
No, no, no, no, no.
The chopper's waiting for us.

266
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:51,544
It's taking us to the airport.
We can go now. We can go now.

267
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:52,920
Yes, but hold on.

268
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:56,215
Hon, I can't just leave.

269
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:59,051
What about Aguas Realty, my business?

270
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:02,304
I can't just leave it. I… I'm sorry!

271
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:05,349
Your mother, your… your grandpa.

272
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,268
He just said yes.

273
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:09,979
He just agreed
that we'd get married next week.

274
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:11,897
Hon…

275
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,525
Hon, relax!

276
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,027
You scared me. I thought Arthur,

277
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,612
-my kidnapper, was back.
-No.

278
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:19,780
-No.
-Hon…

279
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:24,535
Okay. Do you need assurance?

280
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:27,037
Assurance? Is that it, hon?

281
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:32,168
I will get married to you
because I truly do love you.

282
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:34,879
If someone dares to stop our wedding,

283
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:36,922
I won't let them.

284
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:41,343
We'll get married
come hell or high water, hon.

285
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:43,721
Because I love you.

286
00:12:45,347 --> 00:12:47,516
I'm all yours, hon.

287
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,518
That's why I'm getting married to you.

288
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:54,690
I will become
Mrs. Ivy Aguas-Ardiente-Torillo.

289
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,692
I promise you,

290
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:59,111
I will get married to you

291
00:12:59,612 --> 00:13:01,238
because I love you.

292
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,824
Hon, I love you.

293
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,495
Hon, you frightened me.

294
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:11,790
I thought my kidnapper was back again.

295
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:14,293
-No. No.
-Look at me, look at me.

296
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:16,378
[suspenseful music playing]

297
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:17,922
Arnaldo, I love you.

298
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:20,883
I… I… I love you.

299
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:23,552
-I love you so much.
-I'm gonna marry you.

300
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:27,139
[sniffles] I love you so much.

301
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,683
[mumbling]

302
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:32,853
We're getting married, right?

303
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:34,897
Yeah.

304
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:36,440
We're getting married.

305
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,984
-I love you.
-You're mine!

306
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,361
Yes, I'm yours.

307
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:43,364
-You're mine. Okay?
-And you're mine, right?

308
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,950
-You're mine.
-You're mine.

309
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:48,244
[Ivy sniffles]

310
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,453
[whispers] Yes.

311
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,207
[tense music playing]

312
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:10,349
[inaudible]

313
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:14,728
[echoes] <i>Well?!</i>

314
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:18,899
[echoes] <i>Ha!</i>

315
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:21,861
-[grunting, screaming in pain]
-[laughing]

316
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,957
[tense music playing]

317
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,008
[Anna] <i>Jepoy, come in.</i>

318
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:46,635
<i>Come in.</i>

319
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,804
<i>Anna, thanks again for helping me out.</i>

320
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:50,431
<i>You're welcome.</i>

321
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,183
[Jepoy groans]

322
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:56,186
<i>-Is it okay if I stay here?</i>
<i>-Of course.</i>

323
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,271
<i>Thank you.</i>

324
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:59,690
<i>It's just that it's been</i>
<i>a while since we last spoke.</i>

325
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:02,860
<i>And you suddenly texted me,</i>
<i>asking me to have you picked up.</i>

326
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:05,863
<i>Why? Did something happen in Ardiente?</i>

327
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,491
[suspenseful music playing]

328
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,618
[Jepoy groans]

329
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:15,539
<i>Jepoy, I'm not as innocent</i>
<i>as you and Lily think.</i>

330
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:19,335
<i>I know that you work</i>
<i>for Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente.</i>

331
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:22,379
<i>Did he do that to you?</i>

332
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,675
[Jepoy exhales sharply]

333
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:33,265
<i>-Jepoy…</i>
<i>-Anna…</i>

334
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:37,186
<i>Jepoy, whatever it is, you have</i>
<i>to tell me the whole truth.</i>

335
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:40,147
[quietly] <i>Anna, please.</i>

336
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:43,275
<i>Fine. You should get some rest, okay?</i>

337
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,194
[tense music playing]

338
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:50,824
<i>See you later.</i>

339
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:57,915
[door closes]

340
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:02,795
[breathing heavily]

341
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:11,387
[exhales]

342
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:26,485
-[music intensifies]
-[breathing heavily]

343
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,664
<i>Jepoy?</i>

344
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:40,791
<i>Jepoy?!</i>

345
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:48,132
<i>Why do you have those wounds?!</i>
<i>What did they do to you?!</i>

346
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:49,967
[uneasy music playing]

347
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,427
[quietly] <i>Anna…</i>

348
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,929
<i>What happened to you, Jepoy?!</i>

349
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,433
[water sloshing]

350
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,977
<i>Tell me, Jepoy.</i>

351
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:03,063
<i>Did Lily go there</i>
<i>so she could exact her revenge?</i>

352
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:05,774
<i>Jepoy, tell me the truth.</i>

353
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,864
<i>Were the Ardientes behind</i>
<i>the murder of Lily's parents?</i>

354
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:16,702
[in normal voice] <i>Anna…</i>

355
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,539
<i>Lily went to Ardiente to seek revenge.</i>

356
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:22,958
<i>That's the truth.</i>

357
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,127
<i>You're going up against</i>
<i>very powerful people.</i>

358
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:26,712
<i>Just look at what they've done to you.</i>

359
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:27,963
<i>They almost killed you!</i>

360
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,591
<i>Anna, I'm ready to die for Lily!</i>

361
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,094
<i>I'm not done yet.</i>

362
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,097
<i>I'm just getting started.</i>

363
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:39,516
[breathes heavily]

364
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:42,478
<i>I'm going back to Ardiente</i>
<i>to finish them all off.</i>

365
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,563
[breathing heavily]

366
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:49,526
<i>Jepoy, I don't know what I can do to help,</i>

367
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:53,072
<i>but we should treat your wounds first.</i>

368
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:57,326
[tense music playing]

369
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:11,673
[Jepoy groans]

370
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:22,309
[dramatic choral music playing]

371
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:30,359
[breathing heavily]

372
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,210
[music intensifies]

373
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:20,659
[tense music playing]

374
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,957
[Jepoy] <i>Now that I'm back,</i>

375
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:32,045
<i>I will make you suffer</i>
<i>much worse than I did back then.</i>

376
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:34,506
<i>I will take down</i>
<i>every member of your family!</i>

377
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:37,968
<i>I'll start with Arnaldo</i>
<i>so he can't get married to Ivy.</i>

378
00:19:38,051 --> 00:19:42,181
<i>After that, you're next, Julio and Emilia.</i>

379
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:45,184
<i>I will use Jaguar's weapons</i>

380
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:47,811
<i>to wipe out the entire Ardiente clan!</i>

381
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,776
[glass clinking]

382
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:59,656
Could I have your undivided attention?

383
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:06,121
I have a very, very important
announcement to make.

384
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,164
What is it, Papa?

385
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:09,458
[shushes] Emilia, just listen.

386
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:14,671
As you all know, it's been quite a while

387
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:17,799
that we have been preparing
for the forthcoming…

388
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:22,387
Aguas-Ardiente royal wedding.

389
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,807
And I'm very, very happy to inform you…

390
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:29,061
that it is finally going to happen…

391
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:31,438
a week from today.

392
00:20:31,521 --> 00:20:33,065
-[Ivy chuckles]
-[Claire] Really?

393
00:20:33,148 --> 00:20:36,818
Wow! Congratulations! Congratulations!

394
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:39,863
-[Julio] Yes.
-What?

395
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:42,324
What?!

396
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:45,619
No! No, no, no! [pounds on table]

397
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:46,828
No, Papa!

398
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:50,082
Emilia! What's wrong with you? What is it?

399
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:51,917
[tense music playing]

400
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:54,920
[Julio] What?

401
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,550
Can't you see the problem, Papa?!

402
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:02,135
A wedding in a week?!

403
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:04,346
You're all insane!

404
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,515
Especially you, Papa!

405
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:08,767
Me? [scoffs]

406
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:13,397
Yes! A wedding in a week?

407
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,775
How? How, Aunt Claire?
Can you please tell me, Papa?!

408
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:18,360
How?!

409
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:23,115
We don't even have a caterer!

410
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:26,702
I don't have a designer
for my gown yet, Papa.

411
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:28,870
What do I do? That's a big problem.

412
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:31,707
Emilia, you're worried
about your wedding gown?

413
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,917
I'm the one getting married, not you.

414
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:36,295
You act like this is your wedding.

415
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:39,047
We have money, we can find a way.

416
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,592
That's right, and we have
so many people at our disposal.

417
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:43,802
-[Julio] Mm-hmm.
-[Arnaldo] Okay?

418
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:46,221
They will work 24/7 if they have to

419
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,806
just for this wedding to push through.

420
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:49,141
Thanks, hon.

421
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:51,393
[tense music playing]

422
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,857
Okay, if that's the case,

423
00:21:56,940 --> 00:22:00,485
then, go on with the wedding.
I support you.

424
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,863
[tense music playing]

425
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,664
-[sinister music playing]
-Once we reach the casino,

426
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:14,458
go straight to the cashiers.

427
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:18,045
Get everything you can get.
Don't shoot unless necessary.

428
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:20,422
I want this to be a clean job.
Remember this…

429
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:23,884
We're going outside Ardiente,
it isn't our turf.

430
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,011
Understood?

431
00:22:26,344 --> 00:22:27,387
Yes, boss.

432
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:29,264
Let's go.

433
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:33,393
Boss? Maybe I can go with you?

434
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:35,729
I'm ready.

435
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:41,902
[whispering inaudibly]

436
00:22:41,985 --> 00:22:43,862
Just taking my chances, boss.

437
00:22:43,945 --> 00:22:46,615
I'm more useful out there than in here.

438
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:49,910
The boss wants to know

439
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:52,662
if you really want to do this.

440
00:22:53,413 --> 00:22:54,414
Yes.

441
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:56,750
Have some faith, boss.

442
00:22:56,833 --> 00:23:00,921
I swear I'll be your best
and most trusted man.

443
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:04,049
[whispering inaudibly]

444
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:05,509
[man 2] The boss agrees.

445
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:08,178
He says just make sure you don't screw up.

446
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:10,388
Let's go.

447
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,350
[tense music playing]

448
00:23:22,943 --> 00:23:25,612
[music transitions to suspenseful]

449
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:44,131
[horn honking]

450
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:11,575
[music stops]

451
00:24:16,913 --> 00:24:18,915
[tense music playing]

452
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:24,921
That's the group the boss
was talking about.

453
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,299
Congressman Ardiente
wants us to take them out.

454
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:30,802
What are we waiting for? Let's get them.

455
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:32,721
Okay. I'll call for backup.

456
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:38,768
You know what to do.

457
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:42,105
Take your positions inside.
Wait for my signal.

458
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:43,732
-Yes, boss.
-Yes, boss.

459
00:24:46,359 --> 00:24:47,694
[tense music playing]

460
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:51,698
[indistinct conversations]

461
00:25:05,837 --> 00:25:07,255
Sir, we're positive it's them.

462
00:25:07,714 --> 00:25:08,757
We need backup.

463
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:40,705
[tense music playing]

464
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:41,665
[gun clicks]

465
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:43,625
[gun cocks]

466
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:47,837
-[line ringing]
-Jaguar, pick up!

467
00:25:48,588 --> 00:25:49,798
[clinking]

468
00:25:56,429 --> 00:25:57,973
[tense music playing]

469
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:07,649
[line ringing]

470
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:17,784
[suspenseful music building]

471
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:24,666
Boss!

472
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:28,253
They followed us. Julio Ardiente's men.

473
00:26:28,878 --> 00:26:31,298
Boss, it isn't safe to do this now.

474
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:33,008
[tense music playing]

475
00:26:47,564 --> 00:26:49,065
[breathes deeply]

476
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:56,448
[phone ringing]

477
00:26:57,324 --> 00:26:58,158
Boss?

478
00:26:58,241 --> 00:26:59,743
We need to leave right now.

479
00:26:59,826 --> 00:27:01,453
-<i>Abort the mission.</i>
-Okay, boss.

480
00:27:03,621 --> 00:27:05,457
-[clapping]
-[suspenseful music playing]

481
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:54,631
Papa! You're really pushing
through with this wedding?!

482
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:56,132
I thought it was just a sham!

483
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,176
Are we really prioritizing this

484
00:27:58,259 --> 00:27:59,928
over our problem with Lily Cruz?!

485
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:02,722
Papa, you know,
I thought you were a genius.

486
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:04,808
But you know, I'm starting to think

487
00:28:04,891 --> 00:28:07,185
that your brain has been lobotomized.

488
00:28:07,268 --> 00:28:10,271
[scoffs] Lobotomized? Look at me, Emilia.

489
00:28:10,688 --> 00:28:13,691
Do I look like somebody
cut my head open and

490
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:15,443
cut away a part of my brain?!

491
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:20,824
Emilia, I did not stay in power this long

492
00:28:20,907 --> 00:28:23,743
because I am easily fooled by people.

493
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,997
All our enemies… Line them up.

494
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:32,794
Diego, Camia Cruz, Lily Cruz, Jaguar,

495
00:28:32,877 --> 00:28:35,713
and whoever else has gone against us,

496
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:39,801
I promise you, they will all die
after the elections.

497
00:28:40,343 --> 00:28:41,302
Why?

498
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,012
Because we have to wait till then

499
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:47,392
so that no bad publicity will
smear Arnaldo's reputation

500
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:51,354
right before he is elected into office.

501
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:53,940
So, Ivy Aguas will fool us until then?

502
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:59,487
[chuckling] Do I really have
to spell it out for you?

503
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:05,910
Ivy Aguas is not fooling us.
We are fooling her!

504
00:29:06,327 --> 00:29:12,417
We are just using Ivy Aguas
for her money and the good PR

505
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:16,004
she brings with her forthcoming
royal wedding

506
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:21,176
to your son, my grandson,
and yada, yada, yada!

507
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,844
And after all of that,

508
00:29:23,803 --> 00:29:28,683
when we have sucked Ivy Aguas
bone-dry of her money,

509
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:31,686
and her good public image, then maybe,

510
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:34,314
she can be my present to you,

511
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:36,858
and you can do whatever you want with her.

512
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:40,862
Now, is that a clear enough
explanation for you?

513
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:45,867
Or do I have to make
a PowerPoint presentation?

514
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:48,995
No need, Papa. I get it.

515
00:29:49,078 --> 00:29:50,038
[scoffs]

516
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,372
You look surprised.

517
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:53,875
You know, your old man here…

518
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,796
For your information,
I am technology savvy.

519
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:01,341
If only politics didn't steal me away,

520
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:03,635
I could have been…

521
00:30:04,552 --> 00:30:08,139
like Bill Gates and Steve Jobs
rolled into one.

522
00:30:09,599 --> 00:30:13,144
But the call to serve
the people got to me first.

523
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:16,564
-[laughs]
-For public service!

524
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:18,191
Yes!

525
00:30:19,984 --> 00:30:21,194
I'm too good.

526
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:28,952
Okay. Oops!

527
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:31,120
What? Can I come in?

528
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:33,206
No.

529
00:30:34,541 --> 00:30:38,753
You seem to have enjoyed
my last treat for you too much.

530
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:40,797
I just gave you a massage, you know.

531
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:47,554
Hon, you can wait, right?
Just one more week.

532
00:30:49,889 --> 00:30:51,933
Okay. Fine.

533
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,811
I'll see you tomorrow, my future wife.

534
00:30:54,894 --> 00:30:57,939
I'll see you tomorrow, my future husband.

535
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:00,817
I just really hope that…

536
00:31:01,734 --> 00:31:04,612
no one gets in the way
of our wedding again.

537
00:31:05,738 --> 00:31:07,448
If you're talking about my mother,

538
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:09,409
Grandpa's handling her now.

539
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:12,579
Okay.

540
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:14,789
So, stop worrying.

541
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:19,460
I will never let anyone…

542
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:20,712
[kisses]

543
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:22,547
…stop our wedding.

544
00:31:22,630 --> 00:31:23,715
[kisses]

545
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:25,717
[whispers] No one.

546
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:26,801
[giggles]

547
00:31:27,635 --> 00:31:28,595
Hon…

548
00:31:29,804 --> 00:31:30,805
One week…

549
00:31:31,347 --> 00:31:33,725
-[sighs]
-…and I'm all yours.

550
00:31:33,808 --> 00:31:35,310
You can do everything after that.

551
00:31:36,769 --> 00:31:38,021
See you tomorrow.

552
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:40,899
One week.

553
00:31:41,774 --> 00:31:43,401
-Yes.
-Can't wait.

554
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:57,248
[water running]

555
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:05,423
[water running]

556
00:32:09,093 --> 00:32:10,178
[water running]

557
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:23,232
[turns off tap]

558
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:25,568
[exhales]

559
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,112
I'm glad you're here.

560
00:32:30,114 --> 00:32:31,783
Now, we can talk.

561
00:32:32,116 --> 00:32:34,202
[ominous music playing]

562
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:35,578
[clicks tongue] See…

563
00:32:36,579 --> 00:32:38,581
This… Ivy,

564
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:40,541
whom you love so much,

565
00:32:42,585 --> 00:32:43,878
will soon…

566
00:32:44,462 --> 00:32:45,546
be…

567
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:47,757
[whispers] …mine.

568
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:51,719
[in normal voice] Mine. Not yours. Mine.

569
00:32:53,262 --> 00:32:57,517
This woman that challenged you,

570
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:01,270
stimulated every fiber of your being,

571
00:33:02,855 --> 00:33:04,774
will soon…

572
00:33:04,857 --> 00:33:05,900
be…

573
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:07,610
[whispers] …mine.

574
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:11,406
[in normal voice] Not yours. Mine.

575
00:33:12,532 --> 00:33:13,908
And I can't wait.

576
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:16,703
[in growly voice] I can't wait.

577
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:19,747
[whispers] I can't wait.

578
00:33:20,081 --> 00:33:22,834
[in normal voice] I've been
waiting for the longest time.

579
00:33:23,584 --> 00:33:25,003
And soon, she'll be mine.

580
00:33:28,339 --> 00:33:30,383
Ivy Aguas.

581
00:33:32,635 --> 00:33:34,804
Ivy Aguas.

582
00:33:42,228 --> 00:33:45,189
[tense music playing]

583
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,026
Don't worry.

584
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:51,154
I'll take good care of her.

585
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:53,865
I'll make her happy.

586
00:33:54,699 --> 00:33:57,285
I'll make her so happy.

587
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:01,914
[laughing]

588
00:34:04,292 --> 00:34:05,418
[inhales sharply]

589
00:34:08,629 --> 00:34:10,048
[laughs maniacally]

590
00:34:11,758 --> 00:34:12,800
Can't wait.

591
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:16,679
<i>You have such high hopes, Arnaldo.</i>

592
00:34:16,763 --> 00:34:20,975
<i>But I'll make sure</i>
<i>that you will fall just as far.</i>

593
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:23,686
<i>You'll be punished for the things you did</i>

594
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:27,065
<i>very, very soon.</i>

595
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,859
[soft music playing]

596
00:34:30,401 --> 00:34:31,444
Anna…

597
00:34:32,111 --> 00:34:33,321
Yes?

598
00:34:33,404 --> 00:34:34,906
I just want to thank you.

599
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:36,324
What for?

600
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:39,160
For helping out.

601
00:34:39,243 --> 00:34:40,870
For supporting us.

602
00:34:40,953 --> 00:34:42,955
I'd also like to apologize

603
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:46,209
if I didn't immediately
acknowledge your efforts

604
00:34:46,292 --> 00:34:48,711
because I was too busy
worrying about my own daughter.

605
00:34:49,295 --> 00:34:53,299
But I want you to know that
I'm really grateful to you,

606
00:34:53,382 --> 00:34:56,886
and that I'm really happy
you're here with me.

607
00:34:57,804 --> 00:34:59,388
Me too, Auntie Camia.

608
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:03,684
Now that Nanny Carlotta
isn't here anymore,

609
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:06,020
and after everything that's happened,

610
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:10,274
I've come to treat you like family.

611
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:12,902
[both chuckle softly]

612
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,113
[chuckles]

613
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,242
-Let's go home?
-Yes.

614
00:35:19,325 --> 00:35:20,451
[both chuckle]

615
00:35:23,162 --> 00:35:26,666
I know what you're thinking, Auntie.

616
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:32,130
"Poor little loser Emilia."
I'm such a loser, Aunt Claire.

617
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:35,007
I'm going to be drinking my failures away.

618
00:35:35,091 --> 00:35:36,175
[chuckles]

619
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:38,719
I didn't say that, Emilia.

620
00:35:39,387 --> 00:35:40,972
Besides, I thought you and your father

621
00:35:41,055 --> 00:35:43,307
already had a plan for Ivy Aguas.

622
00:35:43,391 --> 00:35:45,810
So, what is this pity party for?

623
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:47,520
Auntie…

624
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:51,107
I will no longer be
the queen of this house.

625
00:35:52,024 --> 00:35:55,778
As it is, look at the way
our men treat me now.

626
00:35:55,862 --> 00:35:57,071
I'm an afterthought.

627
00:35:58,948 --> 00:36:01,409
And by the time Ivy Aguas joins us,

628
00:36:02,118 --> 00:36:05,621
I'll just be a black hole
in the Ardiente solar system.

629
00:36:05,913 --> 00:36:08,624
Of course not. You're the star.

630
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:12,795
From your perspective, Auntie, yes, I am.

631
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:14,005
But the truth is…

632
00:36:14,547 --> 00:36:15,840
[scoffs] …I'm done.

633
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:17,967
I'm so over, Aunt Claire.

634
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:23,139
No. You still have time
to stop the wedding.

635
00:36:23,222 --> 00:36:24,182
[sinister music playing]

636
00:36:24,265 --> 00:36:28,686
Why don't you see how far
Ivy Aguas is willing to go

637
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:31,189
to become part of this family?

638
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:40,198
Thank you, my friend.

639
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:44,660
I trust that your men will stop at nothing

640
00:36:45,411 --> 00:36:48,289
until that bastard is arrested.

641
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:51,792
Thank you.

642
00:36:53,544 --> 00:36:54,670
[exhales]

643
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:03,721
[uneasy piano music playing]

644
00:37:03,804 --> 00:37:04,847
[pills rattle]

645
00:37:23,407 --> 00:37:25,284
I can't die.

646
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:26,702
[suspenseful music playing]

647
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:30,289
Not until I kill that bastard Jaguar.

648
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:34,377
I am Julio Ardiente!

649
00:37:35,211 --> 00:37:39,298
And I will decide when I will die!

650
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:00,987
Boss.

651
00:38:02,154 --> 00:38:03,155
Open it.

652
00:38:07,576 --> 00:38:08,577
[tense music playing]

653
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:09,787
[Jepoy] What's this for?

654
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:11,497
[man 2] If you hadn't warned our boss,

655
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:13,291
we would've gotten into bigger trouble.

656
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:16,919
This money is nothing,
compared to his freedom.

657
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:22,883
That was nothing, boss.

658
00:38:24,844 --> 00:38:26,012
This is too much.

659
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:28,639
Just take it already.

660
00:38:29,056 --> 00:38:33,602
I think you forget just how much
money and weapons we have.

661
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:35,062
This is practically spare change.

662
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:41,819
Boss Jaguar, your group is the only one

663
00:38:41,902 --> 00:38:43,612
that can fight the Ardientes.

664
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:46,782
You can't afford to waste
your money and resources.

665
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:51,787
[tense music playing]

666
00:39:05,551 --> 00:39:07,428
[tense music playing]

667
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:43,297
-[door closes]
-[tense music playing]

668
00:39:45,549 --> 00:39:46,634
Jepoy.

669
00:39:47,843 --> 00:39:49,011
Jepoy, what's that?

670
00:39:53,682 --> 00:39:54,683
Anna.

671
00:39:58,062 --> 00:39:59,105
Look at this.

672
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:02,400
[tense music playing]

673
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:04,110
Jepoy, where did you get all that?

674
00:40:05,486 --> 00:40:06,529
It doesn't matter.

675
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:11,117
Just help me keep these safe.
They're important to my plans.

676
00:40:12,159 --> 00:40:13,702
No, Jepoy, no.

677
00:40:13,786 --> 00:40:15,830
I don't need the money or weapons.

678
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:19,125
Ivy's not going to like this.
You'll just fight again!

679
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:22,795
We're practically siblings now.
Let's not ruin that--

680
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:23,963
I know that, Anna!

681
00:40:27,049 --> 00:40:29,802
Anna, remember that you're in Ardiente.

682
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:32,680
You won't last here
if you put your feelings first.

683
00:40:32,763 --> 00:40:35,141
You have to know the rules of the game.

684
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:39,437
You have to protect yourself at all times.

685
00:40:41,313 --> 00:40:44,567
[tense music playing]

686
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:49,905
Anna…

687
00:40:53,325 --> 00:40:55,202
We aren't kids anymore.

688
00:40:58,205 --> 00:41:00,958
I'll push through with my plans,
even if Ivy's against them.

689
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:03,711
Just what are you going to do, Jepoy?

690
00:41:05,921 --> 00:41:07,465
I'm going to finish off Arnaldo.

691
00:41:07,548 --> 00:41:09,842
[suspenseful music playing]

692
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:12,219
It's time.

693
00:41:21,103 --> 00:41:23,105
-[music fades]
-[birds chirping]

694
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:26,817
Ram, can you tighten it more?

695
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:28,652
How about this, madam?

696
00:41:28,736 --> 00:41:29,737
Tighter.

697
00:41:30,362 --> 00:41:31,363
This tight?

698
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:34,366
Come on, tighten it all the way.

699
00:41:34,450 --> 00:41:36,994
But, madam, the wedding is in a week.

700
00:41:37,077 --> 00:41:39,288
Do it, Ram. Tighten it all the way.

701
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:40,915
I'll magic my way into it
on the wedding day.

702
00:41:40,998 --> 00:41:41,749
-Trust me.
-Yes, madam.

703
00:41:41,832 --> 00:41:42,917
Is everything okay?

704
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:45,169
Yes, Ivy, and from the looks of it,

705
00:41:45,252 --> 00:41:47,963
your wedding is going to be
the most fabulous wedding

706
00:41:48,047 --> 00:41:50,716
of the year here in Ardiente.

707
00:41:50,799 --> 00:41:52,551
I think it'll even be better
than my wedding.

708
00:41:52,635 --> 00:41:55,429
Of course, Emilia. I made sure of it.

709
00:41:55,804 --> 00:41:58,432
I even invited Ardiente TV

710
00:41:58,516 --> 00:42:01,101
to come and cover
the wedding preparations.

711
00:42:01,185 --> 00:42:02,561
And the reporters?

712
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:06,357
They're calling this "the royal
wedding of the century."

713
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:11,529
Wow, the century?
Hmm… So, we'll be live later?

714
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:15,282
Yes. Live on air. Isn't it perfect?

715
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:17,743
Perfect! [chuckles]

716
00:42:18,619 --> 00:42:22,373
Ram, I'm going back.
Make my gown fabulous.

717
00:42:22,456 --> 00:42:24,458
-Yes, madam.
-Give it a long train.

718
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:26,293
-[Ram] That we'll do.
-[Emilia] All right.

719
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:28,128
[chuckles]

720
00:42:28,212 --> 00:42:29,296
[quietly] Perfect.

721
00:42:33,008 --> 00:42:34,051
-Hello, friends!
-[upbeat music playing]

722
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:36,595
Welcome back to <i>Ivy and Arnaldo:</i>

723
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:37,805
<i>The Royal Wedding.</i>

724
00:42:37,888 --> 00:42:39,139
<i>We'll show you</i>

725
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:41,600
<i>the latest developments and preparations</i>

726
00:42:41,684 --> 00:42:44,770
<i>for the coming wedding of the century.</i>

727
00:42:44,853 --> 00:42:45,771
And here she is.

728
00:42:46,146 --> 00:42:47,481
Miss Ivy!

729
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:49,733
-Hi, Phomella. Hello.
-Hello. Hello, Miss Ivy.

730
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:51,318
<i>How are you?</i>

731
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,237
<i>Well, I'm happy.</i>

732
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:55,406
-[Phomella] <i>One week to go.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Yes.</i>

733
00:42:55,489 --> 00:43:00,869
<i>In one week, you're going to be</i>
<i>Mrs. Ivy Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

734
00:43:00,953 --> 00:43:02,454
<i>How does it feel?</i>

735
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:03,789
[tense music playing]

736
00:43:03,872 --> 00:43:05,291
Auntie, is it ready?

737
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:10,004
Yes, Emilia.

738
00:43:10,087 --> 00:43:12,631
[breathes deeply]

739
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:13,799
That's great.

740
00:43:15,050 --> 00:43:17,177
<i>I'm happy. I feel happy.</i>

741
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:20,723
<i>This is the most exciting time</i>
<i>in a woman's life,</i>

742
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:23,225
<i>which is why I'm enjoying it.</i>

743
00:43:23,309 --> 00:43:28,314
<i>I want to thank the viewers at home,</i>

744
00:43:28,397 --> 00:43:31,191
<i>and the people of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

745
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:37,031
<i>Thank you for supporting</i>
<i>the love Arnaldo and I share.</i>

746
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:39,074
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

747
00:43:39,158 --> 00:43:40,951
Miss Ivy, thank you as well

748
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:44,163
for inviting us to interview you

749
00:43:44,246 --> 00:43:46,957
<i>and to cover the wedding preparations.</i>

750
00:43:47,041 --> 00:43:51,462
[Ivy] <i>Of course, Phomella.</i>
<i>We want all of Ardiente</i>

751
00:43:51,545 --> 00:43:56,925
<i>to be updated on what's</i>
<i>happening with our wedding.</i>

752
00:43:57,009 --> 00:43:59,803
<i>And we are very, very excited.</i>

753
00:44:00,846 --> 00:44:03,724
[Phomella] <i>Thank you.</i>
<i>Thank you, Miss Ivy Aguas.</i>

754
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:07,436
<i>Or, wait, should I say, the soon-to-be</i>

755
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:10,856
<i>Mrs. Ivy Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

756
00:44:10,939 --> 00:44:13,442
-[Ivy] <i>That's so nice to hear.</i>
-[Phomella] <i>Thank you.</i>

757
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:19,907
[Jepoy] <i>Now that I have money and weapons,</i>

758
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:24,453
<i>I will stop your wedding</i>
<i>with bullets, Arnaldo.</i>

759
00:44:27,706 --> 00:44:30,000
[Emilia] <i>I prepared</i>
<i>a prenuptial agreement.</i>

760
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:31,919
<i>Should you and Arnaldo decide to separate,</i>

761
00:44:32,002 --> 00:44:34,046
<i>one hundred percent of your assets</i>

762
00:44:34,129 --> 00:44:35,297
<i>will go to Arnaldo.</i>

763
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:38,008
[Claire] <i>You better do it</i>
<i>successfully, Emilia.</i>

764
00:44:38,092 --> 00:44:40,052
<i>Not only will Ivy hit you again,</i>

765
00:44:40,135 --> 00:44:42,221
<i>but Arnaldo and Julio might even kill you.</i>

766
00:44:42,304 --> 00:44:44,515
[Julio] <i>I'm throwing you a stag party</i>

767
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:46,517
<i>on the same day as Ivy's bridal shower.</i>

768
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,727
[Emilia] <i>Just look at what</i>
<i>I prepared for you.</i>

769
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:50,396
<i>We're going to have fun tonight.</i>

770
00:44:50,479 --> 00:44:52,356
[Ivy] <i>Is this part of your plan, Emilia?</i>

771
00:44:52,439 --> 00:44:54,274
<i>Okay, let's have fun.</i>

772
00:44:54,358 --> 00:44:56,360
<i>I can keep up with any of your games.</i>

773
00:44:56,443 --> 00:44:57,403
[muffled exclaim]

774
00:44:57,486 --> 00:44:58,695
[Emilia] <i>How the hell did you get that?!</i>

775
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:00,697
<i>I am Ivy Aguas, remember?</i>

776
00:45:00,781 --> 00:45:03,617
[theme music playing]
